@base <http://example.org/orexis/sensing> .
@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/sensing#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix sosa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
@prefix ssn-system: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/systems/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Orexis sensing, Agent 0.2.0" ;
    rdfs:comment """What the sensing layer of Agent 0.2.0 adds to the sensing package's vocabulary,
    which it otherwise speaks as it stands: the drift and its horizons, what an agent polls and
    what a sensor monitors. Sensing here is the translation row of the agent stack and nothing
    above it — a transport hands it bytes, it makes a number of them and writes one
    sosa:Observation, predicts the number's future with the domain's drifts, and says whether the
    number contradicted what was predicted. It concludes nothing itself: the sides an observation
    is on are revisions, concluded by the three rules this layer registers (rules.ttl beside this
    file) and run by the deliberator over the present. No word of any transport is spoken here.""" .

:ObservationGraph a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf orexis:StateGraph ;
    rdfs:label "Observation graph" ;
    rdfs:comment """One graph per feature and property, holding the whole sosa:Observation the
    sensor last made of it — feature, property, result, instant, sensor, procedure, and the
    instant the device says the result applies to where it says one — from its instant to the
    horizon its period states, replaced whole by the next. Named for what it holds. Beneath
    orexis:StateGraph so that the readers of the present find it by that kind today; that parent
    goes when what a plan may change is the actions' footprint rather than a graph kind.""" .

:readingPointer a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain sosa:Sensor ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "reading pointer" ;
    rdfs:comment """Which value of a decoded document is this sensor's, as a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901).
    A fact about a document and not about a bus, which is why it is sensing's word: two sensors on
    one board share a message and differ only here. Absent, the pointer is /value, which is what
    every single-property device here publishes.""" .

:below a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain sosa:Observation ;
    rdfs:label "below" ;
    rdfs:comment """The observation's result lies under the floor of this range — an
    ssn-system:OperatingRange or ssn-system:SurvivalRange the subject, or an instrument monitoring
    it, states for the observed property. Concluded by this layer's rule as a revision, read by a
    desire's met-test, and written by an effect that predicts a reading. One triple per observation
    and range; nothing is minted per subject.""" .

:inside a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain sosa:Observation ;
    rdfs:label "inside" ;
    rdfs:comment "The observation's result lies within this range, its bounds included." .

:above a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain sosa:Observation ;
    rdfs:label "above" ;
    rdfs:comment "The observation's result lies over the ceiling of this range." .
